WEBVTT

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.340
Oh no, chu!

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.260
There was more than one person
 after Dr. Love, chu!

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.820
Who the hell are you?

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.980
I could ask the same of you.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.230
Who are you people?

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.600
We're with ēlDLIVE.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.540
You're under arrest on suspicion of murder.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:23.310
I see.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.620
Space police, huh?

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.790
Is the guy in the suit over there
 a criminal, then?

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:31.160
Damn it! You ruined my plan!

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.550
Tell me something.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:38.010
Could a plan that needed a geezer 
like this really have succeeded?

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.420
Of course!

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.000
Dr. Love's brain held the key to the gate!

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.430
If I'd had him, I could've gotten 
my hands on some amazing treasure!

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.200
Treasure?

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.420
What does he mean?

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:54.200
It sounds like he needed Dr. Love 
to find what he was looking for.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.900
Oh...

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.530
You had both space police 
and criminals on your tail,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.240
were imprisoned in this tiny room,

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.280
and just when you thought you'd found 
a way out, it was for a treasure hunt?

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:09.250
You had tragically bad luck, Dr. Love.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.630
Shut your mouth, brat!

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.010
Die!

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:16.460
He deflected it?!

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:17.250
A shield?

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.170
I'm good at creating things.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.590
Why, you little...

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.450
Your iris is pretty interesting.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.310
Amber in color, and a very 
characteristic line in the lower half.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.490
I never expected to see it here.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.980
I wish I could've observed it more.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:41.800
It's too bad.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.020
What?

00:01:53.000 --> 00:03:22.970
{OP}

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.100
<b>Something to Believe In: Part 2</b>

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.730
You there!

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.530
Hands above your head.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:31.400
We will not hesitate 
to use force if you resist.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:34.490
Stay here, Officer Kokonose.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:35.570
Yoyosa.

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.680
Chips, Ninotchka, we're going down there.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:42.020
You're under arrest for murder.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:44.110
Murder? Who?

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:44.910
Quiet.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.610
They caught him easily.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:51.990
Yeah, but...

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:56.730
<i>We had to take Dr. Love back with us 
to clear Sonokata of suspicion.</i>

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:00.200
<i>We can't save her now.</i>

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.420
Whoa! I'm so high up!

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:04.380
Why have I been hung out to dry?!

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:06.850
What's going on?

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:07.880
Where am I?

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.970
H-He's alive...

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.090
Hey! You brats!

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:15.430
Who are you? Don't just 
stand and watch! Save me!

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:18.970
Someone's dead!

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:23.950
See? I didn't kill him.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.250
Cuff him too, Nino!

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:27.400
Y-Yoyosa!

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:31.970
What's the meaning of this? 
What did you do to him?

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:33.300
What, you ask?

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:40.020
I used an SPH removal beam to cleanse his body 
of the remote control SPH it absorbed.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.420
Remote control SPH?

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.470
As its name implies,

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.890
it's an SPH that allows the user who emitted it

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:50.900
to control anyone who absorbs it from afar.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:56.020
The characteristic amber membrane 
forms in the eyes of the recipient.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.260
It'd only existed in experimental 
form until now, though.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:05.850
That guy's probably a normal 
Earthling who was being controlled.

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:08.000
Then the mastermind is someone else?

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:08.830
Yeah.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:13.230
Poor Dr. Love. He has 
someone weird on his tail.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:15.430
Look who's talking!

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:18.460
Aren't you the one who 
made a right mess of him?

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:19.950
Yeah.

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:22.430
But that's not a corpse.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.360
It's just waste matter 
from body reconstruction.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.820
During reconstruction,

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:33.890
there was an unexpected split 
between old cells and new.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.600
You could say it was like shedding old skin.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.730
What are you saying?

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:38.910
I mean,

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:42.810
Dr. Love is standing right before you.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.890
You guys rely too much on your eyes.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:51.450
Chips! Compare his SPH to Dr. Love's!

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.700
Yoyosa!

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:57.920
They match, chu!

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.420
He's really Dr. Love, chu!

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.260
No way!

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.120
He looks nothing like the photo!

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:07.890
Are you really Dr. Taklamakan Strangelove?

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:08.630
Yeah.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.170
Why are you all young again?

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:12.760
Isn't that obvious?

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:14.990
The younger, the healthier.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:19.530
Your SPH smells like... a Doltalian?

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:20.640
No.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:23.860
Could you be a descendant of Kurzians?

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:25.270
Y-Yes...

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:26.850
I knew it!

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:28.940
You must boast really powerful kicks, then.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:30.850
W-Well, yeah.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:32.460
This is it.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.400
Your biceps femoris is amazingly supple.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:37.900
It resembles the whiskers of a spica seal.

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.500
The most distinctive feature of 
Kurzians is not their forehead horn,

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:45.620
but the abdominal oblique and femoral muscles 
running down the center of the body.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:44.750
Um...

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:46.960
Right here.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.350
Yes, this is the feeling.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:53.750
Take off your clothes.
 I want to touch it directly.

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.220
Eek!

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:05.100
Oh, right.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:06.540
Sorry.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:10.670
I forgot that lots of humanoid lifeforms 
don't like exposing themselves.

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:12.480
I tend to forget that when I get engrossed.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.230
I'll kick you next time.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.230
Is Dr. Love...

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:18.190
What an amusing man.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:19.270
...a weirdo?

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:21.490
No, he's more of a perv!

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:24.600
Don't tell me, Sonokata also...

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.910
Are you ready, Misuzu?

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.880
Yes, Dr. Love.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.760
All right, let us begin...

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:34.370
Begin our Taklamakan Project.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:37.260
Yes, Dr. Love.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.820
Will you take your clothes off for me, then?

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:45.070
Yes... Dr. Love.

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:55.030
Let's get started on the Taklamakan Project.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:56.910
Or should I say,

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.030
the Tarzan and Jane Project.

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:05.780
That's what the Taklamakan Project was about?!

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:07.470
I don't think so.

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:11.130
Besides, Dr. Love was an 
old man back then, Chuta.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.720
Damn you, Dr. Love!

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.010
You okay over there, rookie?

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:22.240
I-It's nothing.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:26.510
Okay, we've secured Dr. Love, 
so how about we head back?

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:28.390
We were supposed to <i>keep</i> him secure.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.480
Do you mind taking these off first?

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:34.140
Sorry, I forgot.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:41.990
Assistant Inspector Veronica?

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:43.240
Assistant Inspector Chips!

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.490
I'm glad to see you 
in good health, Dr. Love.

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:50.830
With your brain,

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.380
I can open the door to the treasure.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.680
O-Officer Ninotchka?

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:57.660
Her iris...

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:01.370
She's been taken over 
by remote control SPH, too.

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:04.430
You can never be too careful, huh?

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:06.840
N-No way...

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:09.020
But this is weird.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:14.120
Remote control SPH should require a 
convergence of both parties' consciousness.

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:17.290
How'd you take over a member of ēlDLIVE?

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:20.060
I don't mind telling you, Dr. Love.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:33.650
If you come with me, that is.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.990
I'll pass.

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:39.380
Scientists are prone to getting killed 
once they're deemed useless.

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:42.090
You don't have the right to refuse.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:47.490
Now, come along.

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:53.060
This is pretty bad.

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:54.350
Wait!

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:01.070
I'm not letting you take Dr. Love!

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:04.280
Oh, I forgot you existed.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:07.070
Do you have a death wish, Officer Kokonose?

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:11.190
That angelic Officer Ninotchka...

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.120
Dr. Love.

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:18.830
Is there a way to free Officer Ninotchka 
from the remote control SPH?

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:21.700
Could you knock her out?

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:25.300
Meanwhile, I'll repair the 
SPH removal beam and fire it.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:28.810
So we have no choice 
but to fight and win, Chuta.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:29.560
Yeah.

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:33.510
We've gotta do this.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:44.990
<b>Ninotchka</b>

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:50.220
I know it's inappropriate to say this now,

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:52.570
but my heart is racing in excitement.

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:54.830
Seeing you growing on Chuta Kokonose...

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:59.550
Monitaliens are one of my research subjects.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:01.530
R-Right...

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:05.610
Sorry to crush your hopes, 
but you should probably give up.

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:07.290
I mean,

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:09.550
I'm really strong!

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:15.520
Sew her up, Dolugh!

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:17.250
Sympathy!

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.570
That Monitalien hasn't updated.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:32.030
This will be tough.

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.040
Are you okay, Chuta?

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:37.040
What's wrong?

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:39.870
What happened to knocking me out?

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:41.190
I can't do it.

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:42.970
She's in a whole different league.

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:46.010
Chuta, I'm fading.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:47.880
You can't win if you lose confidence.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.560
I know. I know, but...

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:54.850
I can't do anything about my fear!

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.220
Chuta...

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:57.610
Run...

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:00.560
Run away...

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:02.310
Assistant Inspector Veronica?

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.980
You can't handle her...

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:08.910
It's all my fault... I'm sorry...

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.580
What are you saying?!

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:12.120
Run away...

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:14.240
Hurry up...

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:15.870
At least you should get out of this alive!

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:17.840
Run away all by myself?

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:21.040
<i>Even if I escaped with my life,</i>

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:25.880
<i>Veronica, Chips, Dr. Love, 
and Ninotchka here...</i>

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:27.180
<i>...and...</i>

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.560
<i>...Sonokata wouldn't be saved.</i>

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:35.160
<i>I'm the only one who can help them right now.</i>

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:38.680
<i>There's no way I can run!</i>

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:42.480
Hang in there...

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:44.730
Hang in there just a while longer.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:47.570
I promise I'll get you to sick bay.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:51.000
I'm back.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:54.590
Your fading confidence has returned.

00:12:54.590 --> 00:12:55.830
How?

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.480
I don't know the reason myself.

00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:01.090
Even so, I have to believe in myself now.

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:04.100
I mean, I want to save everyone!

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:08.090
You want to save everyone, so you'll believe?

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:11.150
Your confidence is back with a bang.

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:13.080
Okay, let's do this, Dolugh.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:14.430
Yeah, Chuta!

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:16.680
Oh, you want to keep going?

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:23.390
You can't win by running away.

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:25.400
Get behind her.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.980
I can't. She's not taking her eyes off us.

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:29.180
Point.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.240
Chuta, look up.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:34.000
I just got a great idea.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.780
Do you like hide-and-seek?

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:38.110
It's not going to work.

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:39.920
If you won't come out, I'll...

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:50.260
A decoy made out of cables?

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:52.430
Now.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:53.460
Take this!

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:55.220
Just kidding. I can read you 
like an open book.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:02.020
Dolugh!

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:12.230
Not good. Get out of the way, Dolugh!

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:15.630
Are you listening to me?

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:17.780
Dolugh!

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:44.770
The smell of burned SPH...

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:46.470
It's a type of post-death odor.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.850
<i>Hot...</i>

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:57.260
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:58.490
<i>My face is burning.</i>

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:03.240
<i>Huh? I can't speak...</i>

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:04.740
<i>What's happening?</i>

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:05.500
<i>Dolugh...</i>

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:09.500
<i>Dolugh?</i>

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:18.600
<i>Dolugh?!</i>

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:23.360
Monitaliens and their hosts 
receive equal damage.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:26.280
Given the state the Monitalien 
is in, its host must be...

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:32.570
<i>I can't breathe.</i>

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:36.070
Monitaliens are but ancient relics.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:40.330
Dying in agony with its host 
is a fitting end for one.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:44.410
<i>Dying...?</i>

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:47.210
<i>Am I going to die?</i>

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:53.660
<i>Without saving Sonokota, 
Veronica, Ninotchka, or Chips?</i>

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:55.450
<i>Damn it...</i>

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:00.010
Chuta.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:02.840
Is that you, Dolugh?

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:06.520
I've been thinking

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:10.850
about why you averted your eyes 
from the facts and trusted Misuzu.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:12.920
Are you kidding me?

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.610
You're bringing that up now?

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:20.260
I don't think you would've 
done that a short while ago.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:23.260
You've changed ever since 
you joined ēlDLIVE.

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:27.360
I want to know the reasons 
behind any changes in you.

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:30.630
And I think I've figured it out now.

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:35.380
You hoped for Misuzu to be innocent.

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:38.680
That's why you believed in her 
and said she was.

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:43.770
Dr. Isaac hoped for you to protect Misuzu.

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:47.690
That's why he believed in you 
and told you her secret.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:51.270
And in this fight...

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:53.060
I don't know the reason myself.

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:56.850
Even so, I have to believe in myself now.

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:59.650
I mean, I want to save everyone!

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:03.390
...you hoped to save everyone.

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:08.720
That way, you were able to 
really believe in yourself.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:12.830
Yeah, I've finally realized...

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:16.920
...believing in someone 
is an expression of hope.

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:18.670
Hope?

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:21.680
So I'll believe in you, too.

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:23.430
Dolugh?

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:28.160
Because I hope to remain in a symbiotic 
relationship with you, and nobody else.

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:32.390
Killing host's life support process.

00:17:32.390 --> 00:17:34.190
Activating survival program.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.570
It begins.

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:40.450
What's this?

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:43.240
When their hosts are on the verge of death,

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:49.200
Monitaliens us all their remaining energy 
on evolving to escape the danger,

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:51.000
in an attempt to survive.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.500
So you're still trying to live?

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:56.580
I'll break you half-dead freaks!

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:00.840
It deflected?

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:05.880
The goal of a Monitalien's evolution isn't 
to get out of the current predicament.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:09.540
It's to look for a new host 
and transfer over to them.

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:12.030
Next host detected.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:15.680
Calculating necessary evolution 
and transformation.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.860
Attack.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:23.780
Wh-What was that?

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:26.770
Looks like it found the optimal solution.

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:33.420
Transformation confirmed.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.220
Attack.

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:57.420
This almost-scary evolution is the 
highest form of lost Griffith technology.

00:18:57.890 --> 00:19:01.530
Now, it'll just toy with its prey 
until it no longer resists.

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:02.530
Attack.

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:04.990
Not happening!

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:06.700
I'm not losing this body!

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:07.540
Attack.

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:12.500
Attack.

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:16.670
<i>What are you doing, Dolugh?</i>

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:18.550
Host secured.

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:19.750
Attack.

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.170
<i>Stop it, Dolugh.</i>

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:24.660
<i>Stop.</i>

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:26.100
Attack.

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:30.680
Adjusting aim.

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:31.820
S—

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:34.330
<i>I can't speak...</i>

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:35.100
Host secured.

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:35.100
<i>Dolugh.</i>

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:38.650
Come back to your senses, Dolugh.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:39.940
Attack.

00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:41.320
Dolugh!

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:48.280
You know you're better than this!

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:50.450
Sympathy!

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:10.970
Dolugh?!

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:11.970
Chuta!

00:20:11.970 --> 00:20:13.200
Is that really you?

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:15.430
Yep, it's me, Chuta.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:17.220
Thank goodness.

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:19.220
You went back to normal.

00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:22.070
I was seriously lost for a moment there.

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:27.110
You just pulled off a reconnection 
with a Monitalien.

00:20:27.570 --> 00:20:29.400
Reconnection?

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:31.620
I tried to leave you,

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:33.890
and then I connected with you again.

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:35.710
Is that so?

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:38.160
It's no mean feat.

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:41.850
Once a Monitalien prepares to leave its host,

00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:45.060
the chance of bringing it back 
with a strong sympathetic response

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:47.420
is a mere 0.02 percent.

00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:50.100
Strong sympathetic response?

00:20:50.590 --> 00:20:52.820
What if it hadn't worked?

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:54.030
R.I.P., Chuta.

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.850
Wh-What the heck?!

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:58.450
Even if our chances were slim,

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:01.610
we had to do it in order to save everyone.

00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:05.740
Wait, what you said back there...

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:08.680
Believing in someone 
is an expression of hope.

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:11.860
So I'll believe in you, too.

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:16.410
Because I hope to remain in a symbiotic 
relationship with you, and nobody else.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:19.170
You were referring to this?

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:23.960
I believed that you would 
definitely reconnect with me.

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:26.270
You believed in me, too.

00:21:26.270 --> 00:21:29.430
And that sympathy reconnected us.

00:21:32.660 --> 00:21:36.660
You went back to being that 
weak-ass duo? How convenient.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:38.640
No.

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:40.430
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:43.920
I can tell. We're different now.

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:45.280
Isn't that right, Dolugh?

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:47.280
Yeah, Chuta.

00:21:54.960 --> 00:23:24.960
{ED}

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:29.320
Here's the rice-cakes-in-a-soup dish 
you've been wanting to try, Chief.

00:23:29.320 --> 00:23:30.370
It's called zoni.

00:23:30.370 --> 00:23:34.330
But in the dish I fell in love with, 
the soup was darker and sweeter.

00:23:34.330 --> 00:23:36.130
Next time on <i>ēlDLIVE,</i>

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Next Time
Something to Believe in: Part 3</b>

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:37.980
"Something to Believe In: Part 3."

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:40.020
That's red bean soup.
